WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.298
"The Best Daily Dose of Taurine"

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.760
The remarkable trial showing
that taurine supplementation

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.480
improved the lifespan
and healthspan of animals

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.720
used doses
that may far exceed

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.400
the recommended safe
consumption limits in humans.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.120
At the press conference,
the corresponding author said

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.800
that they would not recommend

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.720
people to start taking
taurine supplements

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.600
to try to preserve health
or slow aging.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.160
Not only do we have
no human studies

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.440
showing that kind of benefit,

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.520
we don’t even know
what the potential risks are,

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.680
since we don’t have large,
long-term human safety trials.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.800
In my last video,
I talked about those

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.800
who might be particularly
sensitive to taurine,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.560
and what happens,
at least in the short term,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.040
if we exceed
recommended intakes.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.360
If,
after careful consideration,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.680
you still want to give it a try,

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.160
what source, dose,
and frequency might be best?

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.400
In terms of frequency,
the bump in our blood stream

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.680
only lasts about six hours.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.440
So, we’d presumably
want to split doses

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.800
to maintain higher levels;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.240
for example,
three times a day,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.000
like, at every meal.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.840
What dose?

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.080
Well, just for context,
most people get

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.120
between 40 and 400 milligrams
a day through their diet.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.240
So, that’s like,
a normal, typical daily dose.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.880
If our goal is
to restore youthful levels,

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.720
we’d want to bump our levels up

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.640
from around
the 50-micromole range

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.680
to maybe the 100 or 200 range.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.120
Here’s a study
where participants

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.200
got 400 milligrams a day,

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.160
up at the higher end
of a normal dietary dose,

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.920
for a week, and got levels
into that upper range.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.080
Here, a two-gram daily dose

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.160
also pushed levels
into that target range,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.840
but, unfortunately, studies
are all over the place.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.040
Here’s a good illustration

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.280
of why using
a blood target level

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.720
doesn’t work.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.000
These 10 people were given

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.320
one gram of taurine
three times a day for a month.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.160
First of all,
see how they started

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.520
all over the place,
from 18 to more than 600?

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.720
And after a month,
most of their levels went up,

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.200
but sometimes
they actually went down.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.760
And this measured levels
in the plasma or serum,

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.000
the liquid
part of the blood.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Levels in
the blood cells themselves

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.400
can be hundreds of times higher,

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.880
and levels in whole blood
don’t seem to correlate

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.160
with levels in plasma.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.920
So, should we measure taurine
in whole blood?

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.240
But whole blood levels
don’t move as much

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.160
or even
in any significant amount

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.720
in response to supplementation.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.880
In this study,
researchers gave people

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.440
1.66 grams twice a day,

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.760
shooting up plasma levels
to a thousand,

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:32.880
yet, at the end of the week,

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.680
there was no change
in levels in the muscle,

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.760
based on muscle biopsies.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.400
The body didn’t seem to care
what was happening in the blood

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.960
it kept
the tissue levels stable.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.600
In contrast, when rats
are given taurine,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.320
the levels of taurine
in their muscles go up.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:53.360
So, maybe taurine is like
the NAD-booster debacle?

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.680
You can rewatch my webinar
for a recap,

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.120
but, remember how NAD
also declined with age?

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.960
And restoration
of youthful levels

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.240
with supplements
caused all these

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.000
amazing benefits in lab animals,

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.840
so, a gazillion-dollar

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.560
NAD supplement industry
was born?

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.200
But, when finally
put to the test in people,

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.040
they totally flopped.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.040
And, no wonder.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.960
In rodents,
these supplements

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.600
actually boosted NAD levels
in their tissues,

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.120
but we’re not rodents,

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.960
and the supplements all failed
to raise levels in our muscles.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.680
So, maybe when we have
human trials on taurine,

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.400
they’ll also fail
in the same way.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.600
But maybe not.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.600
For those
who don’t want to wait,

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.840
what dose should we shoot for?

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.760
We really have no idea,

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.480
but from all the human trials
that have been done,

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.920
the most commonly used dose

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.320
in the blood pressure
lowering trials,

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.960
which is probably the best
demonstrated benefit

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.120
that also best lowers

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.440
oxidative stress
and inflammation

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:53.840
is about 1.5 grams a day.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.480
So, that would be 500 milligrams
three times a day.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:59.280
Okay, that’s the dose
and the frequency,

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.680
but what’s the best source?

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:05.127
That’s what I’ll cover, next.

